import Polyfold
/-! Blind formalization of V19_89 (the text's §19.7, Theorem 19.7.29, p. 929 of the Springer 2021
book; 2017: Theorem 19.10).

Text: `𝒜` has a natural polyfold structure for which `P` is a covering functor of polyfolds.

Choices:
- Setting (as in the blind V19_88): universe `0`: groupoidal categories `A`, `B`, a finite-to-one
  covering functor `P : A → B` (Definition 19.7.1; vocabulary `IsFiniteToOneCovering`) and a basic
  construction `Bh = (F̂, 𝓕)` for `P` (Definition 19.7.11; vocabulary
  `CoveringBasicConstruction P`, underlying basic construction `Bh.toBasic` for `B`).
- Hypotheses added: `Bh.toBasic.U.HasClassUniformizers` and `T_{|B|}` (vocabulary
  `Bh.toBasic.natTop hB`) metrizable.  The quoted statement does not repeat them, but `ℬ` is a
  polyfold (with the structure of Theorem 19.5.3 (2)) only under them, and the theorem is the
  conclusion of the preceding construction (Proposition 19.7.26, Theorem 19.7.28), which assumes
  them.  No compatibility hypothesis (the vocabulary's `IsCompatible`) is assumed.
- GCTs: `ℬ` = `(B, T_{|B|})`, the vocabulary's `Bh.toBasic.toGCTOfMetrizable hB hm`, with the
  polyfold structure `BasicConstruction.toPolyfoldConstruction hm` (Theorem 19.5.3 (2));
  `𝒜` = `(A, T_{|A|})`, `T_{|A|}` generated by the collection of Definition 19.7.16 (vocabulary
  `NatOpenA`); its metrizability (needed for `𝒜` to be a GCT) is part of the claim.
- "a natural polyfold structure on `𝒜` for which `P` is a covering functor of polyfolds": I render
  it with Definition 17.8.13: there is a proper polyfold covering functor `𝒜 → ℬ` (vocabulary
  `ProperPolyfoldCoveringFunctor`: a proper covering functor of GCTs with a proper polyfold
  covering structure, whose M-polyfolds `M(Ψ̂, Ψ̂')` with sc-smooth structure maps are the
  polyfold structure of `𝒜`) whose functor is `P` and whose polyfold structure of `ℬ` is the one
  of `(F, 𝓕)`.  I do not tie the structure further to `F̂` ("natural"); see the blind V19_88 for
  that reading of the preceding theorem.
- Nothing looks doubtful to me.
-/
namespace RoundTrip.V19_89
open Polyfold
open GroupoidalCategory

/-- `T_{|A|}`: generated by the collection of Definition 19.7.16. -/
@[instance_reducible]
def topA {A B : GroupoidalCategory.{0}} {P : GroupoidFunctor A.toGroupoidStr B.toGroupoidStr}
    (Bh : CoveringBasicConstruction P) : TopologicalSpace A.OrbitSpace :=
  TopologicalSpace.generateFrom {W | Bh.NatOpenA W}

/-- The GCT `𝒜 = (A, T_{|A|})`, given the metrizability of `T_{|A|}`. -/
def GA {A B : GroupoidalCategory.{0}} {P : GroupoidFunctor A.toGroupoidStr B.toGroupoidStr}
    (Bh : CoveringBasicConstruction P)
    (hA : @TopologicalSpace.MetrizableSpace A.OrbitSpace (topA Bh)) : GCT.{0} :=
  @GCT.mk A (topA Bh) hA

/-- Theorem 19.7.29: `𝒜` is a polyfold and `P` a (proper) polyfold covering functor. -/
def B : Prop :=
  ∀ (A B : GroupoidalCategory.{0}) (P : GroupoidFunctor A.toGroupoidStr B.toGroupoidStr),
    IsFiniteToOneCovering P →
    ∀ (Bh : CoveringBasicConstruction P) (hB : Bh.toBasic.U.HasClassUniformizers)
      (hm : @TopologicalSpace.MetrizableSpace B.OrbitSpace (Bh.toBasic.natTop hB)),
      ∃ hA : @TopologicalSpace.MetrizableSpace A.OrbitSpace (topA Bh),
        ∃ Q : ProperPolyfoldCoveringFunctor (GA Bh hA) (Bh.toBasic.toGCTOfMetrizable hB hm),
          Q.P = P ∧ Q.S.SB = BasicConstruction.toPolyfoldConstruction hm

end RoundTrip.V19_89
